course: dictionary
lesson: 14558
title: Words for machines in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a machine, and the words around them tell you what the machine does. «Please use the photocopier to make ten copies of the worksheet.» The clues are copies and worksheet, so a photocopier must be something that makes paper copies.
explain: Look for clue words like make, copy and jammed. «The photocopier is jammed, so we cannot print the test today.» Jammed means stuck, and a stuck machine cannot work. Try your meaning in the sentence: "The copy machine is stuck, so we cannot print the test" still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: Notice the family of words. «The librarian made a photocopy of the map for me.» The photocopier is the machine, and the photocopy is the paper it makes. When you meet one word from a family, check the others: they often share the same clues.
fact: A photocopier is a machine that makes paper copies of documents or pictures quickly.
fact: A photocopier works with light and toner, which is a fine powder ink.
fact: A photocopy is the paper copy that the machine makes.
fact: Useful phrases are «use the photocopier», «the photocopier is jammed» and «make a photocopy».
fact: You can find a photocopier in schools, offices and libraries.
exercise: «Please use the photocopier to make ten copies of the worksheet.» What is a photocopier? | A room where children eat lunch | A kind of pencil case | *A machine that makes paper copies quickly | A large book of maps
exercise: «The photocopier is jammed, so we cannot print the test today.» What does jammed mean here? | Very loud and busy | Freshly cleaned | Full of jam and sticky | *Stuck, so it cannot work
exercise: «The librarian made a photocopy of the map for me.» Find and copy the word that means the paper copy the machine makes. | librarian | for | *photocopy | map
test: The photocopier uses light and toner. What is toner? | A sticky glue | *A fine powder ink | A small lamp | A kind of paper
test: «Tom wants to make a photocopy of his drawing.» What does Tom want to make? | A new drawing from scratch | *A paper copy of his drawing | A painting on a wall | A photograph of the sky
exam: Where would you most likely find a photocopier being used every day? | *A school office | A swimming pool | A bakery selling bread | A farm field
